Description: Add NC30 (Pi 5 column-tiled P010) Fourcc mapping for 10-bit HEVC
 Pi 5 rpi-hevc-dec exposes V4L2_PIX_FMT_NV12_10_COL128 (fourcc 'N','C','3','0')
 on its CAPTURE MPLANE queue when the input stream is 10-bit (HEVC Main 10).
 .
 Diagnostic evidence (mpv strace on Pi 192.168.1.114, 2026-05-05):
 .
   ioctl(15, VIDIOC_ENUM_FMT, {index=0,
     description="10-bit Y/CbCr 4:2:0 (128b cols)",
     pixelformat=v4l2_fourcc('N','C','3','0')}) = 0
   ioctl(15, VIDIOC_S_FMT, {... pixelformat=NC30,
     plane_fmt=[{sizeimage=4147200, bytesperline=1620}], num_planes=1}) = 0
 .
 ENUM_FMT for 10-bit input lists ONLY NC30 at index 0 (no NV12 fallback).
 Without NC30 in chromium's recognized fourcc list,
 V4L2VideoDecoder::SetupOutputFormat() rejects every enumerated CAPTURE
 format and aborts decode init with "Failed to pick an output format" --
 chromium falls back to software HEVC decode for 10-bit streams.
 .
 This patch mirrors the NC12 plumbing already established by patches
 0002 / 0007:
 .
   * media/gpu/chromeos/fourcc.{h,cc}: register NC30 as a known
     single-plane multi-planar fourcc, mapped to PIXEL_FORMAT_P010LE
     (the 10-bit equivalent of NV12 in chromium's media-layer
     vocabulary).
   * media/gpu/chromeos/video_decoder_pipeline.cc:
     DefaultPreferredRenderableFourccs() -- add NC30 alongside NC12.
   * media/mojo/services/gpu_mojo_media_client_linux.cc:
     GetPreferredRenderableFourccs() -- add NC30 at the front for the
     production renderable-format path.
 .
 EXPERIMENTAL / KNOWN INCOMPLETE (same caveats as NC12)
 NC30 is BCM2712 column-tiled 10-bit YUV in 128-byte-wide column tiles,
 NOT linear P010. Mapping NC30 -> PIXEL_FORMAT_P010LE lies about the
 buffer layout to chromium's media-layer code. Likely outcomes at
 runtime, mirroring the NC12 progression:
   * DMA-buf import succeeds and visual output is shown (clean or
     corrupt) -- expected; lets us characterise the next blocker on
     the 10-bit path.
   * Or import fails downstream with a specific error -- specific
     failure point to triage next.
 .
 Either way this advances 10-bit HEVC past the current static block.
 Full SAND128-modifier zero-copy 10-bit will require GPU-side P010
 column-tiled handling, scoped as a follow-up.
Author: chromium-rpi-hevc <build@chromium-rpi-hevc>
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-05-05

--- a/media/gpu/chromeos/fourcc.cc
+++ b/media/gpu/chromeos/fourcc.cc
@@ -36,6 +36,7 @@ std::optional<Fourcc> Fourcc::FromUint32
     case MT2T:
     case BGR4:
     case NC12:
+    case NC30:
     case AR24:
     case Q08C:
     case Q10C:
@@ -200,6 +201,13 @@ VideoPixelFormat Fourcc::ToVideoPixelFor
       // memory layout is column-tiled and will need GPU-side SAND128
       // modifier handling to actually render correctly.
       return PIXEL_FORMAT_NV12;
+    case NC30:
+      // EXPERIMENTAL: BCM2712 column-tiled 10-bit YUV from rpi-hevc-dec
+      // (V4L2_PIX_FMT_NV12_10_COL128). Reported here as P010LE so the
+      // media layer's bit-depth / stride math accepts it. Underlying
+      // memory layout is column-tiled 10-bit and will need GPU-side
+      // SAND128 modifier handling to actually render correctly.
+      return PIXEL_FORMAT_P010LE;
     case BGR4:
     case AR24:
       return PIXEL_FORMAT_ARGB;
@@ -302,6 +310,7 @@ std::optional<Fourcc> Fourcc::ToSinglePl
     case MT2T:
     case BGR4:
     case NC12:
+    case NC30:
     case AR24:
       return Fourcc(value_);
     case YM12:
@@ -339,6 +348,7 @@ bool Fourcc::IsMultiPlanar() const {
     case MT2T:
     case BGR4:
     case NC12:
+    case NC30:
     case AR24:
     case Q08C:
     case Q10C:
